 For example, the compiler might determine that a value is not used after some point in the code, and then not even generate code to compute that value. The result is that the value is never assigned.

```c
int a, b, c;
...
if (a == 1) {
    b = 2;
    c = 3;
}
...
```

Now consider this code:

```c
int a, b, c;
...
if (a == 1) {
    b = 2;
    c = 3;
}
